WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.080 --> 00:00:05.069
Speaker 1: So last week, we talked about President
Joe Biden's declining approval rating and

00:00:05.069 --> 00:00:09.850
it's been a significant decline as of last
week, Joe Biden's approval rating was down

00:00:09.850 --> 00:00:11.320
about 16 percent.

00:00:11.320 --> 00:00:18.150
Now, that's 16 percent, not 16 points from
about 55 to 46.

00:00:18.150 --> 00:00:23.369
My sense last week was that Joe Biden's approval
rating would probably continue down before

00:00:23.369 --> 00:00:25.390
it might recover, depending on what happens.

00:00:25.390 --> 00:00:27.840
But my sense was we hadn't yet seen the bottom.

00:00:27.840 --> 00:00:32.110
The reason that I thought that was that the
full scope of the Afghanistan situation wasn't

00:00:32.110 --> 00:00:33.680
yet in last week's polling.

00:00:33.680 --> 00:00:38.770
And what I mean by that is that the polling
we looked at early last week was taken mostly

00:00:38.770 --> 00:00:43.930
before the suicide attack by ISIS at Kabul
Airport in Afghanistan.

00:00:43.930 --> 00:00:48.250
And in fact, I pointed out last week that
Joe Biden's approval decline actually started

00:00:48.250 --> 00:00:52.090
in July before any of the Afghanistan situation
got going.

00:00:52.090 --> 00:00:56.640
But certainly the Afghanistan situation was
not helping and that we would probably see

00:00:56.640 --> 00:00:58.340
a further decline.

00:00:58.340 --> 00:01:05.760
Indeed, in the last week, Joe Biden's approval
has exactly as expected, continued to decline

00:01:05.760 --> 00:01:11.280
not dramatically more than last week, but
the downward trajectory is clear and he's

00:01:11.280 --> 00:01:15.590
now down to just a hair over 45 percent approval.

00:01:15.590 --> 00:01:20.000
We care more about the average of polls than
about any individual poll.

00:01:20.000 --> 00:01:22.720
We want to look at sort of the general direction.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:29.290
But there are now some individual polls showing
Joe Biden at only 42 percent and 44 percent

00:01:29.290 --> 00:01:32.470
approval and there may be even more of a decline.

00:01:32.470 --> 00:01:34.340
So what are the important notes here?

00:01:34.340 --> 00:01:35.340
Why is this happening?

00:01:35.340 --> 00:01:36.340
What are we looking for?

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.340
What do we expect?

00:01:37.340 --> 00:01:39.090
Two of the major drags on.

00:01:39.090 --> 00:01:46.950
Joe Biden's approval right now are covid resurgence
with Delta four, which really Republican governors

00:01:46.950 --> 00:01:52.830
and antiwar anti boxers and anti maskers are
to blame more than Joe Biden's policy.

00:01:52.830 --> 00:01:56.020
Biden's policy has been get people vaccinated,
keep schools safe.

00:01:56.020 --> 00:02:00.050
But I don't deny that ultimately the buck
stops with Biden and he has said that.

00:02:00.050 --> 00:02:05.910
So that's one drag which at a sort of nitty
gritty level is actually the fault of mostly

00:02:05.910 --> 00:02:06.910
Republicans.

00:02:06.910 --> 00:02:09.170
The second drag is Afghanistan.

00:02:09.170 --> 00:02:15.800
So if covid improves by November of twenty
twenty two for the midterms, I believe people

00:02:15.800 --> 00:02:18.430
will have forgotten about Afghanistan in general.

00:02:18.430 --> 00:02:23.740
Foreign policy impacts voting less than domestic
policy, and Biden himself is not actually

00:02:23.740 --> 00:02:24.740
on the ballot.

00:02:24.740 --> 00:02:30.330
You can see November of 22 as a sort of referendum
on Joe Biden for sure.

00:02:30.330 --> 00:02:35.330
But this may not really be the end of the
world for Joe Biden and Democrats in November

00:02:35.330 --> 00:02:36.330
of twenty two.

00:02:36.330 --> 00:02:42.780
Now, for a comparison to prior presidents,
Joe Biden's approval today is still seven

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:48.060
points higher than Trump's at this point in
their presidencies.

00:02:48.060 --> 00:02:54.390
But below both where Barack Obama was at this
point in his presidency and below were George

00:02:54.390 --> 00:02:59.480
W. Bush's approval was at this point in his
presidency.

00:02:59.480 --> 00:03:00.480
So what does it mean?

00:03:00.480 --> 00:03:01.480
What's next?

00:03:01.480 --> 00:03:06.870
Really, there's no change from what we outlined
last week on Afghanistan.

00:03:06.870 --> 00:03:12.640
Execution aside, Joe Biden got us out of a
war that we needed to get out of.

00:03:12.640 --> 00:03:13.780
That's good.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:15.070
That's the big story.

00:03:15.070 --> 00:03:20.620
The big story is Bush got us into Afghanistan.

00:03:20.620 --> 00:03:22.750
Obama didn't get us out.

00:03:22.750 --> 00:03:24.380
Trump didn't get us out.

00:03:24.380 --> 00:03:25.380
Biden got us out.

00:03:25.380 --> 00:03:26.580
Were there execution mistakes?

00:03:26.580 --> 00:03:27.580
Of course.

00:03:27.580 --> 00:03:28.580
And we've talked about it.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:29.780
There's no doubt about that.

00:03:29.780 --> 00:03:34.709
But I don't believe that the big narrative,
which is Biden got us out and it didn't go

00:03:34.709 --> 00:03:37.310
perfectly, is going to impact 2022.

00:03:37.310 --> 00:03:43.349
The tough part comes where Biden now really
needs a big success.

00:03:43.349 --> 00:03:49.560
But the lower his approval rating, the less
likely that Republicans are going to be incentivized

00:03:49.560 --> 00:03:56.099
to work with him unless he makes some gigantic
compromises, for example, on infrastructure,

00:03:56.099 --> 00:04:02.050
which might turn Biden's victory into a Pyrrhic
one, a Pyrrhic victory, one in which you sustain

00:04:02.050 --> 00:04:06.390
so much damage in getting the victory that
in practice it's a question as to whether

00:04:06.390 --> 00:04:07.790
really it's a victory.

00:04:07.790 --> 00:04:09.890
So it's this vicious circle.

00:04:09.890 --> 00:04:13.740
Biden needs a big accomplishment to Buie,
his approval rating.

00:04:13.740 --> 00:04:18.629
But having a lower, lower approval rating
reduces the pressure on Republicans to actually

00:04:18.629 --> 00:04:22.059
work with Joe Biden because his approval rating
is already lower.

00:04:22.059 --> 00:04:26.590
And the expectations from the American public
that Republicans work with him may also be

00:04:26.590 --> 00:04:27.590
diminished.

00:04:27.590 --> 00:04:32.599
Joe Biden is expected to address the nation
tomorrow, Thursday, about covid.

00:04:32.599 --> 00:04:35.749
There's a question as to whether he will be
announcing new guidelines, new restrictions,

00:04:35.749 --> 00:04:38.199
mandates, whatever the case may be.

00:04:38.199 --> 00:04:41.249
We will see what kind of an audience that
gets.

00:04:41.249 --> 00:04:44.900
We will see if it does anything for his approval.

00:04:44.900 --> 00:04:50.309
And I don't know what time that is tomorrow,
but my intention is to cover it live on YouTube,

00:04:50.309 --> 00:04:51.319
Twitter and Facebook.

00:04:51.319 --> 00:04:53.139
So I hope you will join me.

00:04:53.139 --> 00:04:58.460
It's been already kind of previewed by the
Biden administration that there is not going

00:04:58.460 --> 00:04:59.620
to be an announcement on.

00:04:59.620 --> 00:05:03.419
A federal vaccine mandate tomorrow.

00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:08.229
There was some theorizing and theorizing is
even probably too generous a term.

00:05:08.229 --> 00:05:13.240
There was some speculation by some on the
right that tomorrow is the day that Biden

00:05:13.240 --> 00:05:15.669
announces a vaccine mandate.

00:05:15.669 --> 00:05:17.410
And that's it for many of them.

00:05:17.410 --> 00:05:18.410
What that means, I don't know.

00:05:18.410 --> 00:05:20.569
It sounds violent, but OK.

00:05:20.569 --> 00:05:24.940
But the administration has already said that
is not that is not the plan.

00:05:24.940 --> 00:05:27.339
And in so many words that this is not their
wording.

00:05:27.339 --> 00:05:28.339
This is mine.

00:05:28.339 --> 00:05:32.820
But it was made clear that Joe Biden is not
announcing a vaccine mandate tomorrow, but

00:05:32.820 --> 00:05:53.569
he will be announcing something and we'll
see what that does and we'll continue to track

00:05:53.569 --> 00:07:12.469
his approval rating.

